-- title:
--   Partial Atkin–Lehner automorphism on L·ℚ(X₁(Mp)) with conjugation laws
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M\ge 1$ a natural number with $p\nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))=$ `LaurentSeries L` equal to `laurentBaseChange L (x1FunctionField (M * p))`, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb L` of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $j\in K$ have underlying Laurent series `coeffEmb L jq`, the image of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Then there exists an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ with four properties. (1) $\sigma j$ has underlying series `coeffEmb L (qExpand ℚ p jq)`, the series obtained from $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $p$, i.e. $j(q^p)$. (2) For every $f$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull (M * p)` — the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the series $j(q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $Mp$ — whose image under `coeffEmb L` lies in $K$, $\sigma$ sends that image to the image of `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p f`, where `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p` is a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of that field interchanging $j(q^d)$ and $j(q^{dp})$ for all nonzero $d\mid M$ (the identity if none exists). (3) For all $d,d'$ coprime to $Mp$ with $d'\equiv d \bmod M$ and $d'd\equiv 1 \bmod p$, and all $L$-algebra automorphisms $\theta_d,\theta_{d'}$ of $K$ which, on elements with equal underlying Laurent series, agree with `baseChangeAut L (diamondAut (M * p) d)` resp. `baseChangeAut L (diamondAut (M * p) d')` on `laurentBaseChange L (x1FunctionField (M * p))`, one has $\sigma\circ\theta_d\circ\sigma^{-1}=\theta_{d'}$, read as equality of underlying Laurent series at every $x\in K$; here `diamondAut (M * p) d` is a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of the function field satisfying the diamond-operator characterisation `IsDiamondAut` (identity if none exists), and `baseChangeAut L` is its chosen base change compatible with `coeffEmb L`. (4) For every $s\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ and every $b$ coprime to $p$ with $s\zeta=\zeta^b$, every $b'$ coprime to $Mp$ with $b'\equiv 1 \bmod M$ and $b'\equiv b \bmod p$, every ring automorphism $S_s$ of $K$ acting on underlying series by applying $s$ to coefficients, and every $\theta_{b'}$ representing `baseChangeAut L (diamondAut (M * p) b')` as above, one has $S_s\circ\sigma\circ S_s^{-1}=\sigma\circ\theta_{b'}$, again as equality of underlying Laurent series at every $x\in K$.
--
--   This packages the partial Atkin–Lehner automorphism $w_p$ at the level of function fields: an $L$-automorphism of $L\cdot\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$ sending $j$ to $j(q^p)$, restricting to the Atkin–Lehner involution on the field generated by the $j(q^d)$, and satisfying the two conjugation rules describing its interaction with the diamond operators and with the Galois action on the cyclotomic coefficient field. It is the input to the level-$p$ involution statement, where the chart-stability and branch-moving clauses are added.
